# FRONTEND · what must not enter the build context
#
# Short and hand-kept on purpose: everything in fl_frontend/ not listed here reaches the builder,
# so this list answers "what does the image see?". Add a line when something here is a secret, a
# machine-local artifact, or output the image rebuilds for itself. `**/` where a name can appear
# at any depth: a bare `*.log` matches the context root alone and would leave src/**/*.log in the
# context, while `**/` also matches zero directories, so the root copy needs no second line.

# Matched by shape rather than inventory: a rule holds whether or not anything matches it now,
# because a credential inside an image is a failure nobody sees until it ships. The containers
# take their environment from compose's env_file at run time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
# The deliberate trade: an `.npmrc` usually carries pnpm configuration, so one added later to
# shape the install would never reach `deps` and the build would not say why. Excluded anyway --
# a registry token in a shipped image is found too late.
**/.npmrc

# Reinstalled by the deps stage from the lockfile, and the host tree is built for another platform,
# so copying it in would be both wrong and the largest thing in the context.
**/node_modules/

# Build output. The builder writes its own; the host's copy could only shadow it.
.next/

# Machine-local tool state, rewritten by every `pnpm typecheck` and every `pnpm lint` (~700 KB and
# ~320 KB). In the context either makes the builder's `COPY . .` layer key depend on whether anyone
# ran the tool.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

**/*.log

# buildkit receives both by other means; copying them in only invalidates layers.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
